{{Quote|Kublop Springs, my hometown.|[[Nash Durango]], to the Jedi Initiates|<ref name="The Young Jedi">{{YJA|The Young Jedi}}</ref>}}
'''Kublop Springs''' was a town located on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Tenoo]]. Near the town was a [[Jedi]] [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|outpost temple]].<ref name="Caper" /> Kublop Springs was founded by [[Kaliah Kublop]], the first person to visit Tenoo. A [[Kaliah Kublop statue|statue]] of her could be found near [[Hap's Sap Tap]].<ref name="The Junk Giant" />

The [[pirate]] [[Cyrus Vuundir|Taborr Val Dorn]] once tried to steal [[fruit]] from the marketplace, but [[Jedi Initiate]]s [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], and [[Nubs]] were able to prevent the robbery.<ref name="Pirate Showdown" />

By [[33 BBY]],<ref name="Living Force date">According to {{InsiderCite|224|Launchpad}}, ''The Living Force'' takes place one [[Standard year|year]] before the events of {{Film|I}}, which equates to [[33 BBY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> the Jedi public events in Kublop Springs were recalled by [[Jedi Master]] [[Yaddle]], who described them as an inspiration for the [[Jedi Order]]'s bicentennial celebration on the planet [[Kwenn]].<ref name="The Living Force">''[[The Living Force]]''</ref>
{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Kublop Springs was first named in the description of the sixth ''[[Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures]]'' short, which released on [[April 24]], [[2023]].<ref name="Pirate Showdown" />

